  <h2 style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;Support &amp; Resistance</h2>

  <h3>📘 Definition</h3>
  <p>Support &amp; Resistance are key price levels where the market tends to react. 
  <b>Support</b> is a level where buyers step in to prevent price from falling further. 
  <b>Resistance</b> is a level where sellers step in to prevent price from rising further.</p>

  <h3>🧠 Understanding</h3>
  <p>Think of Support as a floor and Resistance as a ceiling. Price often bounces off these levels. 
  Identifying them helps you find entry and exit points and predict market behavior.</p>

  <h3>📊 Types</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Horizontal Support &amp; Resistance:</b> flat levels from past swing highs/lows.</li>
    <li><b>Dynamic Support &amp; Resistance:</b> moving averages or trendlines.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>🔍 Identification (Step-by-Step)</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Look for previous swing highs and lows.</li>
    <li>Draw horizontal lines at key levels where price reversed multiple times.</li>
    <li>Use trendlines or moving averages for dynamic S/R.</li>
    <li>Check higher timeframe for stronger support/resistance zones.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>⚠️ Conditions</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Level must have been tested at least twice.</li>
    <li>Should align with higher timeframe structure.</li>
    <li>Stronger if combined with order blocks or FVGs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>🧪 How to Trade</h3>
  <p><b>Buy Setup:</b>&nbsp;</p><p></p><ul style="text-align: left;"><li>Price approaches support</li><li>&nbsp;confirm with order block or FVG</li></ul><p></p><p></p><ul style="text-align: left;"><li>enter buy</li><li>stop loss below support.</li></ul><p></p>
  <p><b>Sell Setup:</b></p><p></p><ul style="text-align: left;"><li>Price approaches resistance</li><li>&nbsp;confirm with order block or FVG</li><li>&nbsp;enter sell</li><li>stop loss above resistance.</li></ul> <p></p>

  <h3>❌ Mistakes</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Trading S/R in sideways/confused markets.</li>
    <li>Ignoring higher timeframe alignment.</li>
    <li>Using weak levels with little reaction history.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>🧠 Psychology</h3>
  <p>Support &amp; Resistance gives a mental map of market behavior, prevents impulsive trades, 
  and increases confidence by showing where price is likely to react.</p>

  <h3>📌 Summary</h3>
  <p><b>Support &amp; Resistance</b> = key levels where price reacts.<br />
  <b>Support:</b> floor for price → potential buy zone.<br />
  <b>Resistance:</b> ceiling for price → potential sell zone.<br />
  Confirm with order blocks, FVGs, and higher timeframe alignment.</p>
</div>
