  <h2 style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;Liquidity</h2>

  <h3>📘 Definition</h3>

  <p>Liquidity is the availability of orders in the market that can be taken by smart money. 

  It represents areas where retail traders place their stops and limit orders, creating **liquidity pools**.</p>

  <h3>🧠 Understanding</h3>

  <p>Think of liquidity as the “fuel” smart money needs to move the market. 

  Price often moves to **grab liquidity** (stop hunts) before continuing in the real direction. 

  Understanding liquidity helps traders identify **high-probability entry zones**.</p>

  <h3>📊 Types</h3>

  <ul>

    <li><b>Stop-Loss Liquidity:</b> Orders placed above highs or below lows.</li>

    <li><b>Limit Order Liquidity:</b> Buy or sell orders waiting at key levels.</li>

    <li><b>Hidden Liquidity:</b> Orders in areas not obvious to retail traders.</li>

  </ul>

  <h3>🔍 Identification (Step-by-Step)</h3>

  <ol>

    <li>Look for clusters of swing highs/lows where retail stops are likely placed.</li>

    <li>Observe sudden moves that trigger these stops (stop hunts).</li>

    <li>Mark liquidity zones above resistance or below support.</li>

    <li>Combine with order blocks, FVGs, and market structure for confirmation.</li>

  </ol>

  <h3>⚠️ Conditions</h3>

  <ul>

    <li>Occurs near swing highs/lows, key support/resistance.</li>

    <li>Usually follows a false break or inducement.</li>

    <li>Higher timeframe alignment increases reliability.</li>

  </ul>

  <h3>🧪 How to Trade</h3>

  <p><b>Buy Setup:</b></p><p></p><ul style="text-align: left;"><li>Price grabs liquidity below support</li><li>&nbsp;then reverses</li><li>&nbsp;Enter buy after confirmation with order block or FVG</li><li>Stop loss below liquidity zone.</li></ul><p></p>

  <p><b>Sell Setup:</b>&nbsp;</p><p></p><ul style="text-align: left;"><li>Price grabs liquidity above resistance</li><li>then reverses</li><li>Enter sell after confirmation with order block or FVG</li><li>Stop loss above liquidity zone.</li></ul><p></p>

  <h3>❌ Mistakes</h3>

  <ul>

    <li>Trading liquidity zones without confirmation from structure.</li>

    <li>Ignoring higher timeframe alignment.</li>

    <li>Confusing normal volatility with real liquidity grabs.</li>

  </ul>

  <h3>🧠 Psychology</h3>

  <p>Understanding liquidity helps you trade:with smart money instead of against it, 

  reduces fear of fake moves, and improves confidence in entries and exits.</p>

  <h3>📌 Summary</h3>

  <p><b>Liquidity</b> = orders that smart money targets.<br />

  Look for stop-loss and limit order pools above resistance or below support.<br />

  Confirm with order blocks, FVGs, and market structure before entering trades.</p>

</div>
