  <h2 style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;Fibonacci Retracement</h2>

  <h3>📘 Definition</h3>
  <p>Fibonacci Retracement is a tool used to identify potential;support and resistance levels. by measuring the distance between a swing high and swing low. Common retracement levels are <b>23.6%, 38.2%, 50%, 61.8%, and 78.6%</b>.</p>

  <h3>🧠 Understanding</h3>
  <p>Fibonacci helps traders find areas where price may **pause, reverse, or continue the trend**. 
  It’s widely used with market structure, order blocks, and FVGs to locate high-probability entries.</p>

  <h3>📊 Types</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Classic Fibonacci Retracement:</b> drawn between a swing high and low.</li>
    <li><b>Extended Fibonacci Levels:</b> for projecting future price targets.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>🔍 Identification (Step-by-Step)</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Identify the latest swing high and swing low on the timeframe you are trading.</li>
    <li>Draw Fibonacci retracement from low to high (for bullish trend) or high to low (for bearish trend).</li>
    <li>Observe key retracement levels where price reacts.</li>
    <li>Combine with order blocks, FVGs, or S/R for entry confirmation.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>⚠️ Conditions</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Use swing points from the relevant timeframe.</li>
    <li>Confirm with other tools (order blocks, FVG, S/R).</li>
    <li>Trend must be clear; avoid applying Fibonacci in highly choppy markets.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>🧪 How to Trade</h3>
  <p><b>Buy Setup:</b>&nbsp;</p><p></p><ul style="text-align: left;"><li>Price retraces to Fibonacci level near support/order block</li><li>&nbsp;Enter buy after confirmation</li><li>&nbsp;Stop loss below swing low.</li></ul><p></p>
  <p><b>Sell Setup:</b></p><p></p><ul style="text-align: left;"><li>Price retraces to Fibonacci level near resistance/order block</li><li>Enter sell after confirmation</li><li>Stop loss above swing high.</li></ul> <p></p>

  <h3>❌ Mistakes</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Using Fibonacci without confirmation from structure or order blocks.</li>
    <li>Relying on exact level instead of zone.</li>
    <li>Trading in sideways or unclear trends.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>🧠 Psychology</h3>
  <p>Fibonacci levels help you plan trades with confidence, 
  anticipate price reactions, and avoid impulsive entries.</p>

  <h3>📌 Summary</h3>
  <p><b>Fibonacci Retracement</b> = potential support/resistance levels.<br />
  Common levels: <b>23.6%, 38.2%, 50%, 61.8%, 78.6%</b>.<br />
  Always confirm with market structure, order blocks, or FVGs before entering trades.</p>
</div>
