  <h2 style="text-align: center;">Trading Terminologies</h2>

  <h3>📘 Introduction</h3>

  <p>Trading Terminologies are the essential words used in the financial markets. 

  Understanding them helps you read charts, execute trades, and follow strategies correctly.</p>

  <h3>📊 Basic Terms</h3>

  <ul>

    <li><b>Asset:</b> Anything traded (Crypto, Forex, Stocks).</li>

    <li><b>Pair:</b> Two currencies traded together (e.g., EUR/USD).</li>

    <li><b>Price:</b> Current value of an asset.</li>

    <li><b>Volatility:</b> Speed of price movement.</li>

  </ul>

  <h3>📊 Order &amp; Execution Terms</h3>

  <ul>

    <li><b>Order:</b> Instruction to buy or sell.</li>

    <li><b>Market Order:</b> Instant buy/sell at current price.</li>

    <li><b>Limit Order:</b> Buy/sell at a specific price.</li>

    <li><b>Stop Loss (SL):</b> Limits losses.</li>

    <li><b>Take Profit (TP):</b> Locks in profit.</li>

    <li><b>Spread:</b> Difference between bid and ask.</li>

