  <h3>📊 Risk Management Terms</h3>

  <ul>

    <li><b>Risk:</b> Potential loss in a trade.</li>

    <li><b>Reward:</b> Potential profit.</li>

    <li><b>Risk/Reward Ratio:</b> Comparison of risk to reward.</li>

    <li><b>Leverage:</b> Borrowed capital to increase trade size.</li>

    <li><b>Margin:</b> Required collateral for leveraged trades.</li>

  </ul>

  <h3>📊 Market Behavior Terms</h3>

  <ul>

    <li><b>Trend:</b> Direction of the market (Bullish, Bearish, Sideways).</li>

    <li><b>Bullish:</b> Market going up.</li>

    <li><b>Bearish:</b> Market going down.</li>

    <li><b>Liquidity:</b> Ease of buying/selling.</li>

    <li><b>Volume:</b> Number of trades in the market.</li>

  </ul>

  <h3>📊 Advanced / SMC Terms</h3>

  <ul>

    <li><b>Market Structure:</b> Highs and lows pattern.</li>

    <li><b>Order Block:</b> Institutional buying/selling zone.</li>

    <li><b>FVG:</b> Price imbalance.</li>

    <li><b>Liquidity Grab:</b> Stop hunt movement.</li>

    <li><b>Inducement:</b> Trap to attract traders before real move.</li>

  </ul>

