  <h2 style="text-align: center;">Risk Management</h2>

  <h3>📘 Definition</h3>

  <p>Risk Management is the process of identifying, analyzing, and controlling the potential losses in trading. 

  It ensures that no single trade or series of trades can wipe out your capital.</p>

  <h3>🧠 Understanding</h3>

  <p>Proper risk management protects your account from large losses and allows you to trade consistently over time. 

  It involves controlling trade size, setting stop losses, and maintaining a healthy risk/reward ratio.</p>

  <h3>📊 Key Concepts / Types</h3>

  <ul>

    <li><b>Risk per Trade:</b> Percentage of your capital you are willing to risk on a single trade.</li>

    <li><b>Position Size:</b> The number of units or lots to trade based on your risk.</li>

    <li><b>Stop Loss (SL):</b> Limit potential losses by exiting trades at a predetermined price.</li>

    <li><b>Take Profit (TP):</b> Set exit levels to lock in profits.</li>

    <li><b>Risk/Reward Ratio:</b> Compare potential loss to potential gain, usually 1:2 or higher.</li>

    <li><b>Leverage Control:</b> Using leverage wisely to avoid overexposure.</li>

    <li><b>Diversification:</b> Spreading risk across multiple trades or assets.</li>

  </ul>

  <h3>🔍 How to Apply</h3>

  <ol>

    <li>Decide your maximum risk per trade (e.g., 1–2% of total capital).</li>

    <li>Calculate position size based on SL distance and risk percentage.</li>

    <li>Set stop loss and take profit levels for every trade.</li>

    <li>Maintain a consistent risk/reward ratio (1:2 or higher).</li>

    <li>Adjust leverage to match your risk tolerance.</li>

    <li>Diversify trades to reduce total exposure.</li>

  </ol>

  <h3>⚠️ Conditions / Rules</h3>

  <ul>

    <li>Never risk more than your predetermined percentage per trade.</li>

    <li>Always use SL and TP to manage risk.</li>

    <li>Do not over-leverage your account.</li>

    <li>Review past trades to improve risk management strategies.</li>

  </ul>

  <h3>🧪 How to Use in Trading</h3>

  <ul>

    <li>Before entering a trade, calculate position size and set SL/TP.</li>

    <li>Maintain proper risk/reward ratios to protect profits.</li>

    <li>Adjust risk dynamically based on market conditions and volatility.</li>

    <li>Use diversification to avoid large losses from a single market event.</li>

  </ul>

  <h3>❌ Mistakes</h3>

  <ul>

    <li>Trading without a stop loss.</li>

    <li>Over-leveraging beyond your risk tolerance.</li>

    <li>Ignoring position sizing.</li>

    <li>Poor risk/reward ratio selection.</li>

    <li>Failing to diversify trades.</li>

  </ul>

  <h3>🧠 Psychology</h3>

  <p>Proper risk management reduces stress, prevents emotional decisions, and helps you trade consistently. 

  Traders who control risk are less likely to panic during market volatility.</p>

  <h3>📌 Summary</h3>

  <p><b>Risk Management</b> = protecting your capital.<br />

  Key points: <b>risk per trade, position size, SL/TP, risk/reward ratio, leverage, diversification</b>.<br />

  Always calculate risk before trading and maintain discipline for long-term success.</p>

</div>
